ich serves as a call to Arms rhaenyra  even calls Allison to enter supporters  the greens for the first time this week  as she discusses the precariousness of  her current position with Damon that's  combined with the fact that we finally  see the princess of Dragonstone in Black  means this familial Civil War the greens  versus the blacks has truly reached the  point of no return prior to episode 7  rhaenyra was usually costumed in some  combination of creamy white gold and red  these colors are meant to symbolize if  not quite her innocence than at least  her youth or perhaps her optimism the  Targaryen colors are red and black but  black is more prominent the fact that  she's attending Lena's funeral gives her  a reason to change into a darker color  scheme but this is also the installment  in which rhaenyra and Allison themselves  come to blows it's also notable who else  is wearing black the King Damon Corliss  Raines Lenor useris and luceris Allison  and her three children are still cloaked  in a darker shade of Hightower green  even at these somber proceedings episode  7 begins with Lena's funeral and ends  with rhaenyra and Damon's wedding but  three more potential future Patrol dolls  are either referenced or subtly teased  throughout the episode aegon scoffs at  having to marry his idiot sister Elena  who's muttering to herself about black  and green spools and Dragons of Flesh  weaving dragons of thread if it wasn't  clear last week it is this week Elena is  a dreamer who appears to be able to  foretell the future though we're not  sure if she's aware of her own power yet  in the previous episode she said Eamon  would have to close an eye to get a  dragon which comes to pass  you will have a dragon one day  he'll have to close an eye that aegon  and Elena are to Wed means Allison's got  her way and refused rhaenyra's proposed  match with jaserys which had police the  king viewers can probably guess based on  Prince aegon's attitude toward his  sister alone that theirs won't be a  happy marriage this also means joserus  is free to marry someone else his mother  tells him to comfort his cousins Bela  and Reina he's mourning the loss of his  own father Harwin strong so the best he  can do is stand next to them Bala grabs  his hand in solidarity later when aemon  steals vegar it's luceris who first  defends Reina whose egg is yet to hatch  and who wanted to claim pagar against  his half-brother weddings in the Game of  Thrones Universe are conducted in  accordance with a variety of religious  and cultural Traditions one element of  many ceremonies is The Binding of hands  we see a septon wrapped Joffrey and  marjorie's hands in strips of white  fabric as they recite the customary vows  of the faith of the seven through Bran  Stark we witness rhaegar Targaryen and  lyanna Stark do the same before they're  much happier though equally short-lived  marriage for their own wedding Damon and  rhaenyra have decided to blend the rites  of old valyria with the customs of  modern day Westeros most targaryens  aren't particularly religious at least  not when it comes to the new Gods George  R.R Martin doesn't go into much detail  about Targaryen weddings except that  they are wed by Blood and fire while  earlier in episode 7 blood trickled from  Rainier's curled hand after Allison  slashed her with the catspaw dagger and  her wedding to her uncle she willingly  slices open her Palm Damon does the same  and the brand new husband and wife find  their hands impress their cut lips  together in what appears to be a  Valyrian blood ritual we don't know what  words Damon and Lena exchanged but  rhaenyra and lenor's quick wedding after  Joffrey's murder was done in accordance  with the papers 7. in contrast Damon and  rhaenyra's ceremony is conducted in  Valyrian this creates yet another source  of tension between the blacks and the  greens who were practicing devotees of  the faith of the seven episode seven  ends with a shocking Cliffhan